  "asr_text": "We all want to value the time we spend learning, but even when we want the same thing, what we stand to lose if a decision is wrong and how much responsibility we must take on are different. One bag can't hold everyone's idea of what counts as good. The power to decide how money is spent, the power to shape the classroom, and the responsibility to keep daily life going—even when people have little say in decisions, the burdens they carry are no lighter. Even if what they need to protect matters deeply, they may not get to take part in the decision. Before we close the bag, are we shutting out even the acceptance someone has not yet found the words to express?",
